REVIEW.md

# Claude / GSD local harness state (private — do not distribute)
# Excludes the entire .claude/ dir: GSD framework install, memory, hooks,
# settings, worktrees, scheduled tasks, install-state JSON. None of it
# belongs in the published repo. (Prior to v1.57.2 this exclude was a
# narrow set of 3 subdirs and the rest leaked into a PR; widening to the
# whole dir is the durable fix.) The .claude-plugin/ dir is separate
# (legitimate plugin manifest) and stays tracked.
.claude/

# Phase 28.8 D-16: maintainer-local Cursor Marketplace publish state.
# Tracks application status across submit → review → publish cycle.
# Never committed; ground truth for `scripts/install.cjs --doctor`.
.cursor-plugin/marketplace-state.json

# Phase 28.8 (Plan 28-8-X1): Tier-2 distribution bundle output —
# built from scripts/skill-templates/ via scripts/build-distribution-bundles.cjs.
# Not committed: it's a deterministic build artifact, rebuilt on demand.
# Polish v1.57.3: dist/claude-code/ was a byte-identical duplicate of skills/
# (Claude Code reads ./skills/ via package.json#skills). Removed to drop
# ~120 files of pure duplication from the npm tarball. All dist/ contents
# are build-only artifacts now.
dist/
dist/*.tgz

# v1.58.0 attempted to gitignore skills/ (build artifact regenerated by `prepare`).
# That broke the Claude Code marketplace install path — Claude Code git-clones the
# plugin (NOT `npm install`), so post-clone `./skills/` was absent and the plugin
# failed to load any skill. v1.58.1 reverts the gitignore: skills/ stays tracked as
# a committed build artifact. scripts/skill-templates/ remains the canonical editable source
# (no source/ wrapper, that win sticks); the build:skills:check drift gate enforces
# `committed skills/ == compiled(scripts/skill-templates/)`. The `prepare` lifecycle still runs
# `build:skills` on `npm install` (so contributor checkouts stay in sync after edits)
# but the committed copy is what Claude Code consumes.

# macOS cruft anywhere in the tree
**/.DS_Store

# Phase 30 (Plan 30-04): /gdd:report-issue payload drafts.
# Already covered by `.design/` above, but called out explicitly so
# the Phase 30 D-04 invariant (drafts persist on disk locally, never
# enter the repo) is visible at the .gitignore layer. Drafts can
# contain pseudonymized stack traces — privacy-private state.
.design/issue-drafts/

# Phase 31 (Plan 31-01) D-09: raw Figma extract cache. The off-context
# puller (scripts/lib/figma-extract/pull.cjs) writes raw REST responses
# (can be 200+ MB per file) here; reproducible from pull.cjs, never
# committed. Canonical raw-cache root for the whole figma-extract pipeline
# — siblings (31-02 digest, 31-06 receiver, 31-09 health) use this path.
# (digest/ artifacts may be committed; only raw/ is ignored — D-09.)
.figma-extract-cache/
# Phase 31 (Plan 31-10) D-09 clarifier: the COMMITTED figma fixtures and
# baselines are NOT under .figma-extract-cache/, so they are NOT matched by
# the rule above and remain tracked — the offline e2e + baseline tests need
# test/fixtures/figma/*.json and test/fixtures/baselines/phase-31/*.txt in-repo.
# (Listed here only as documentation; no ignore/un-ignore directive needed.)

# Phase 31.5 (Plan 31-5-9.5, D-16): esbuild-compiled SDK bin artifacts.
# `npm run build:sdk` (and `prepack`) bundle the three TS-entry bins to
# self-contained `.js` SIBLINGS so the packed/installed tarball ships RUNNABLE
# JavaScript (raw `.ts` cannot run under --experimental-strip-types from inside
# node_modules). The `.ts` are the source of truth; these `.js` are build
# artifacts regenerated on every pack and cleaned by `postpack`. Listed
# EXPLICITLY (not a `sdk/**/*.js` glob) so the hand-written, committed
# `sdk/primitives/*.cjs` + `*.d.cts` are never at risk.
sdk/cli/index.js
sdk/mcp/gdd-state/server.js
sdk/mcp/gdd-mcp/server.js
